%% alt: Sequence diagram of two ways to turn a text rent column into numbers. With astype(float) pandas converts every value; if all convert you get a float64 Series, but one bad value such as n/a raises a ValueError and nothing is kept. With to_numeric and errors coerce, each value that fails becomes NaN, no error is raised, and you must count the NaN you did not expect.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant Y as Your code
  participant P as pandas
  participant S as Text column
  Y->>+P: `df["rent"].astype(float)`
  P->>S: convert every value
  alt every value converts
    S-->>P: numbers
    P-->>Y: a float64 Series
  else one value fails, like n/a
    S-->>P: cannot convert
    P-->>-Y: ValueError, nothing is kept
  end
  Y->>+P: `pd.to_numeric(rent, errors="coerce")`
  P->>S: convert each value
  loop for each value that fails
    S-->>P: cannot convert
    P->>P: store NaN instead
  end
  P-->>-Y: float64 Series with NaN, no error
  Note over Y,P: the NaN you did not expect are now invisible
  Y->>Y: count them: `(out.isna() & raw.notna()).sum()`
